 "text": "Resources - Allied Cooperative\nMain\nUtilities\nAgronomy\nSeed Products\nCrop Nutrition\nPrecision Ag\nCranberry Division\nContacts & Locations\nPest Pros\nEnergy\nPropane\nOrder Propane\nRefined Fuels\nGrease And Lubricants\nEnergy Team & Service Areas\nFeed\nFeed Services\nFeed Products\nFeed Quality\nSafety Information\nContacts & Locations\nGrain\nCash Bids\nFutures\nOptions\nGrain Marketing\nGrain Policies\nGrain Settlement ACH Payments\nLocations & Hours\nText Message Sign Up\nRetail\nAce Hardware\nConvenience Stores\nCountry Stores\nLawn Care Services\nNAPA Auto Parts\nMauston Tire Shop\nStratford Tire and Service Center\nInfo Center\nMembership Information\nHistory\nNewsletters\nCommunity Involvement\nScholarships\nShow & Grow Rewards\nContact Us\nCareers\nCredit\nResources\nNews\nWeather\nLocations\nEmployee Login\nCustomer Login\nEFC Login\nNews\nWeather\nResources\nCredit\nLocations\nCareers\nContact Us\nCustomer Login\nEFC Login\nEmployee Login\nMember Resources\nMember Information\nWe believe there are many reasons to join our cooperative - great service, competitive pricing, and an array of member benefits are just a few.\nAs a farmer's cooperative, voting privileges at Allied Cooperative are limited to active producers of agriculture products who meet the minimum purchase requirements. However, all members agriculture or non-agriculture -- qualify for member benefits.\nJoining the cooperative is easy. Simply complete a membership application/credit application and return to Allied Cooperative.\nDownload Credit Application\nFarmer Wellness\nFarming is more than a job -- it's a way of life. But the pressures that come with it can be overwhelming. Commodity prices, unpredictable weather, rising costs and financial stress can weigh heavily on farmers and their families. It's important to remember that you are not alone. Feeling stressed, discouraged, or overwhelmed is something many people in agriculture experience, and reaching out for support is a strong and important step.\nIf you or someone you know is struggling, help is available. You can get free, confidential and immediate support any day, any time through the 24/7 Farmer Wellness Hotline. Trained helpline representatives understand the unique challenges farmers face and are available to provide ongoing, long-term support whenever you need it. Don't let the stress bring you down -- there are people who care and want to help. Call 1-800-901-2558 to talk with someone today.\nAllied Cooperative\n540 S Main St.\nAdams, WI 53910\nP: 800-247-5679\nE: info@allied.coop\nAgronomy\nEnergy\nFeed\nGrain\nRetail\nAbout Us\nLocations\nNews\nWeather\nCareers\nContact Us\nPrivacy & Terms of Service | Site Map\n© 2026 Allied Cooperative. All rights reserved\nSearch for:\nMinimum 3 character allowed.",
